From 66aeca57b4ba6952789f1cf7a70bae0518870d5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 14:54:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix regressions from Supabase migration refactor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

### Motivation
- Repair TypeScript/runtime regressions introduced while refactoring Supabase integration to a multi‑org/RPC flow so the app compiles and runtime API shapes line up across UI and libs.
- Restore correct prop/variant shapes for shared UI primitives and normalize embedded Supabase relation shapes to avoid unsafe casts.

### Description
- Fixed session page stream components to pass the required `selectedId` into `Inbox` and `PulseFeed`, and corrected action lookups to use `inject_id` consistently.
- Reworked role/org context wiring: added `lib/profile.ts` and `lib/org.ts`, updated `app/components/useRoleContext.ts` to use RPCs (`ensure_profile_bootstrap`, `getMyProfile`, `listMyOrganizations`, `set_active_org`, `set_my_active_role`) and expose `refresh`, `switchRole`, and `switchOrg` helpers.
- UI/API compatibility fixes: adapted `AppShell` to the updated `AppTopbar`/`MobileSidebar` props, added `OrgSwitcher` component, updated `RoleSwitcher` to use context helpers and membership ceilings, and corrected `Button` variant values (`primary`/`danger` → supported variants).
- Normalized Supabase embed shapes and org scoping across libs (`lib/profile.ts`, `lib/sessions.ts`, `lib/scenarios.ts`, `lib/facilitator.ts`, `lib/sessionsRuntime.ts`, `lib/users.ts`) to include `org_id` scoping and safe array/object handling for embedded relations.

### Testing
- Ran `npm run build` repeatedly during fixes to iterate on TypeScript errors and prop mismatches; build now proceeds past the earlier TypeScript failures caused by the refactor.
- Final build run still fails prerender in this environment due to missing environment variables `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, so full static export could not be validated here.
- No automated test failures were introduced by these changes in the local build attempts (TypeScript regressions fixed).
